    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d685">

                <pb facs="1184" n="1090" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg1090"/>

                <head>No. 685.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-02-07"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 7, 1887</date>.
                        (Received March 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 286.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with my dispatch No. 257, of
                    October 19, 1886, and your reply No. 171, of 11th November, I have the honor to
                    inclose a copy (in translation) of the dispatch received from the Sublim Porte,
                    and likewise a copy of my reply to it.</p>
                <p>1 learn from the missionaries that, as a result of the visit of Rev. Mr. Filian
                    to Constantinople, he has obtained permission to continue preaching) which he
                    had been prevented from doing.</p>
                <p>I have insisted on the right of Br. Herrick and our missionaries to visit that
                    city and preach, notwithstanding the smallness of the congregation.</p>
                <p>Hoping that my action will meet your approval,</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pendleton King.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d685-a1.xml" xpointer="d685-a1"/>
